    'mpdris2': '#!/usr/bin/env python3\n"""Run the official mpDris2 with the s2udio stream-art extension.\n\nThe official mpdris2-git package cannot show album art for non-file\nstreams: its find_cover() returns None for http(s) URLs. s2udio writes\nthe resolved YouTube/Jellyfin thumbnail to ~/.cache/rmpc/mpris-art\n(expected-source guarded), and this shim loads the *installed official*\n/usr/bin/mpDris2, teaches find_cover() to serve that file for stream\nURLs (cache-busted by mtime so KDE media controls re-fetch on stream\nchange), then runs the official main body unmodified.\n\nSecond extension — desktop-notification toggle: s2udio\'s Settings\npanel can turn the mpDris2 "now playing" popup off; the shim wraps\nNotifyWrapper.notify() to consult s2udio\'s mpdris2-notify.json state\nfile on every notification (absent = enabled, the upstream default).\n\nThird extension — seek hardening: MPD cannot seek HLS audio streams\n(they answer "Not seekable"), and the official Seek/SetPosition would\ncrash the daemon: seekid() only exists via __getattr__ -> call(), which\ncatches CommandError as MPDError and calls reconnect(), releasing the\nD-Bus name and killing mpDris2. The shim installs a real seekid()\nmethod (shadows __getattr__; direct client call; CommandError is a\nno-op that logs "Seek rejected by MPD (stream not seekable)") and wraps\nthe Seek/SetPosition D-Bus methods (carrying their _dbus_* contract\nthrough dbus-python\'s _method_lookup()) to no-op on CommandError and on\nstream statuses with no \'time\' timeline (KeyError). The seekable-looking\ntimeline is kept on purpose — seeks on the MPD path just no-op.\n\nFourth extension — call() hardening: MPD answers benign CommandErrors\nfor playback commands in the wrong state (next/previous while stopped ->\n"Not playing"); the official call() treats those like a lost connection,\nreconnects and releases the D-Bus name, which makes desktop media\ncontrols drop the player entirely. The shim wraps call() to no-op on\nCommandError (logged) while keeping real connection errors on the\nofficial reconnect path.\n\nFifth extension — socket_callback() hardening: mpDris2 sets a 5 s socket\ntimeout at connect(), and the official idle-event fetch has no handler,\nso a TimeoutError while MPD is busy kills the daemon (the MPRIS entry\nvanishes and media keys stop working). The shim wraps it to reconnect on\nany socket/MPD error instead of dying.\n\nVersion-guarded: the find_cover/update_metadata/notify extensions are\nversion-guarded (if the installed mpDris2 changes shape, the shim runs\nit unpatched rather than breaking MPRIS — unpatched also means the\nnotification toggle is inert and notifications stay on, the upstream\ndefault); the seekid method is safe to install unconditionally because\nassigning a real method only shadows the __getattr__ delegation. This\nis a compat shim over the official package — no patched copy of\nmpDris2 is shipped or installed.\n\nsetup.sh installs this to ~/.local/bin/s2u-mpdris2 and points\nmpDris2.service at it via a drop-in. Any extra argv is passed through to\nthe official parser (e.g. --use-journal).\n"""\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n# mpDris2\'s allowed_tags coerces mpris:length to dbus.Int64; the\n# injection below must do the same or dbus-python packs the plain int as\n# Int32 and overflows for any duration > ~2147 s. The import is guarded\n# so the shim stays importable (and unit-testable) without python-dbus;\n# the host that runs the real bridge always has it.\ntry:\n    import dbus\nexcept ImportError:\n    dbus = None\n\n# Round 19: s2udio-only cache files default to ~/.cache/s2udio (the\n# pre-round-19 ~/.cache/rmpc location is used when it still holds the\n# files — migration).\ndef _s2u_cache(file):\n    env = os.environ.get("S2U_CACHE_DIR")\n    if env:\n        return os.path.join(env, file)\n    new = os.path.expanduser("~/.cache/s2udio/" + file)\n    legacy = os.path.expanduser("~/.cache/rmpc/" + file)\